Hi @JaapKeuter ,

option_len is declared as uint8. and more over, after reading the packet contents, option_len value is decremented resulting in breaking while loop once the option_len reaches 0 or below that.

while(option_len > 0)
{
     proto_tree_add_item(tree, hf_extreme_ps_prem_proxy_addr, tvb, offset, 6, FALSE);
     **option_len-=6;**
     offset+=6;
}
break;

Still confused how this goes to infinite loop. Do you mind sharing your thought on the failed scenario.

Also, do you suggest me to check for the Maximum captured packet length (tvb_captured_length(tvb)) and return from function before entering while?
